  "body": "Conjecture: open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.recover_json_object fails to distinguish two replies that its documented rule requires it to tell apart. The rule states: \"The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text\". Reply A is: ```python\n{\"a\":1}\n```\n{\"a\":2}. Reply B is: {\"a\":2}. For reply A the rule requires the recovered object to be {\"a\":1}, because the only code fence holds that object. For reply B the rule requires {\"a\":2}, because there is no fence and the last top-level object is {\"a\":2}. But the function returns {\"a\":2} for both. Its fence regex only matches fences with optional json or JSON language, so the python fence in reply A is not placed in the fenced pool; the top-level scan then sees both objects and returns the last, {\"a\":2}. The observation that would show this conjecture false is running recover_json_object on reply A and getting {\"a\":1}, or getting different recovered objects for the two replies.",
